    Persist the delivery row FIRST at enqueue time (durable intent — the queue is delivery optimization, not the record), then enqueue queue job with deliveryId. enqueueWebhookDelivery (worker helper) moves to shared module (packages/db or apps/api lib? worker uses it; ses-events api path also needs it — Phase 1 SES events enqueue webhooks? Not wired). Better shared: packages/db/src/webhook-deliveries.ts? Actually delivery worker should live in apps/worker; the enqueue helper shared via @calder/db functions is fine. Events for webhooks: at enqueue time, look up enabled webhooks for project subscribed to event type (webhookEventEnum filter via events array JSON contains). Insert one delivery row per webhook (or one row per event with webhookId... row per webhook ✓ shape). Then enqueue job(s).
    Consumer in worker: queue.process on webhook:deliver: load delivery row + webhook row (url, secret decrypt?? choose: secrets are ENCRYPTED (AES-GCM) since they must be usable for HMAC signing — hashed won't work for signing. M0.3 webhook-secrets.ts: check actual scheme) → build payload JSON envelope {id, type, created, data:{...}} → sign: t=timestamp,v1=hex(hmac_sha256(secret, t + "." + body)) (Resend/Stripe-style) with header calder-signature → POST with 10s timeout → record result (status delivered + latency + deliveredAt | increment attemptCount + nextAttemptAt backoff | status failed(dead-letter) at max attempts). Backoff schedule: 5s, 30s, 2m, 10m, 30m, 2h, 6h (8 attempts). The queue's own retry... but "session tries of consumer": process job → attempt counter per job attempt; simpler to let the QUEUE retry the whole job (InMemory job attempts) — delivery.attemptCount mirrors job.attempts; on final failure mark dead. With Redis queue in prod same contract. No cron needed. nextAttemptAt = computed (informational).
    Replay (M3.2): POST /v1/webhooks/:id/deliveries/:deliveryId/replay → creates a NEW delivery row with same payload (new id; replay dedupe: replaying is explicit user action; idempotent event id keeps consumer-side dedupe via payload.id) + enqueue.
    Dashboard UI: /webhooks page: registry + per-webhook expandable delivery log (last 20: status glyph, event, latency, attempts, error, replay button). Server action replayDelivery + rotateSecret (rotation backend exists? webhooks route rotation — check). SDK snippet page lists signing verify snippet.
    SSRF guard: on webhook URL create/update: HTTPS-only + deny private ranges (resolve? Server-side DNS pinning is over-much; basic: blocklist localhost/127./10./172.16/192.168/169.254/::1 by hostname literal + known metadata IP) at registry write (API layer + dashboard action layer).
    Timing-safe verify snippet in docs + SDK page.
    Tests: signature vectors (unit), backoff schedules (unit), delivery worker logic w/ stubbed fetch (integration-ish unit), registry SSRF denial (unit/api test), replay dedupe (integration when pg back).

