No worries at all! Let me answer your three questions directly, then finish up what's in flight.

1. Your separate calder-api Vercel deployment — absolutely still needed. In fact my very last fix was specifically to keep it working. Here's the architecture:

    apps/api (your calder-api Vercel deployment) = the public REST API (/v1/emails, /v1/domains, /v1/webhooks…) that your customers' SDKs call. It deploys as a serverless function, and it needs a bundler (bundle-serverless.mjs) because Vercel's runtime doesn't compile our workspace TS sources — my last edit was making that bundler handle the new subpath imports Phase 4 introduced. Nothing about that deployment is being removed; the webhook work and the domain-verification work both land in it.
    apps/dashboard (separate Vercel app) = the control UI your customers log into.
    apps/web = the public marketing/docs site.

So: keep calder-api on Vercel exactly as-is. If anything, Phase 3/4 made it more load-bearing (it's where webhook signing and domain verification now live).

2. Phases left: 6 total. Phases 0–4 are done (0 hygiene, 1 delivery truth, 2 send integrity, 3 webhooks — all green-committed; 4 domain trust is built and green, ~1 step from committing). Remaining: Phase 5 (dashboard truth — search/pagination, suppressions manager, template CRUD, CI gates against dead links/fabricated numbers) and Phase 6 (auth hardening + control-plane completion).

