# Phases 0–6 + Official SDK Libraries
Recovered aggregate of the completed Calder roadmap work (Phases 0–6) plus official client libraries, transferred from the previous session workspace via a verified patch (sha256 fea32f1b…, 1,268,023 bytes, applied with `git am --3way`, no conflicts).
## Highlight blocks
- Phase 6 M6.1 auth hardening (ADR-040): H4 OAuth link rule closed (takeover impossible via unverified provider email), DB progressive lockout before scrypt (30s→30m, unit-tested), reset revokes all sessions + clears lockout, session inventory + revoke in settings (UA/IP/last-seen), OTP v2 peppered HMAC (purpose+email bound, dual-accept window), bounded magic-link consume, mandatory CRON_SECRET in prod, Redis fixed-window limiter with loud degraded fallback (ADR-041), migration 0022_auth_hardening.
- Phase 6 M6.2 control truth pass: plan grants founder-only + audited mandatory reason; role grants reason-prompted; audiences counted via honest joins; settings presence checks read reality; abuse ladder restyled; server-only guard; full §11 re-audit in docs/PHASE6-RE-AUDIT.md (all H + M items closed).
- Phases 0–5 (per ROADMAP status blocks): API/provider/worker substrate, auth, plans/usage, Gmail+SES transports, webhooks engine, domain verification, control plane, dashboards, docs.
- SDKs (ADR-042): packages/sdk-node (14 tests), sdks/python (16 tests), sdks/ruby+php beta, dashboard SDK hub updated.
## Verification
- pnpm -r test: 242 passed, 0 failed (10 packages + worker/api/dashboard)
- dashboard production build: clean
- python pytest: 16 passed
## Post-merge ledger (tracked, not in this PR)
- Apply migrations 0018–0022 (incl. 0022_auth_hardening) on live Postgres
- Prod envs: CRON_SECRET, ADMIN_API_KEY, AUTH_SECRET (32+ chars), REDIS_URL
- Integration suites on live PG; Flow-D DNS/AWS pass
- SDK registry publishes per sdks/README.md

