  git fetch origin transfer-two
  git show origin/transfer-two:transfer-final.b64 > transfer-final.b64

  echo "838ad0c8a95ce094313233f0975d49dbee64b4d238e5542e99c82527aae10963  transfer-final.b64" | sha256sum -c -
  # ^ pasted-text integrity check. MUST print OK.

  base64 -d < transfer-final.b64 | zcat > calder.patch
  # if base64(1)/zcat look alien on your platform: python3 -c "import base64,gzip,sys; sys.stdout.buffer.write(gzip.decompress(base64.b64decode(open('transfer-final.b64','rb').read())))" > calder.patch

  wc -c calder.patch           # MUST be 1159159
  echo "3599cab039c24264543b3f33182e1736295abec15e2e2cb479a1fd5591fedcee  calder.patch" | sha256sum -c -   # MUST print OK
  head -1 calder.patch         # MUST start with: From cc35a0ac4ac76dab07ba17b9ad80df93eae4b953

  rm transfer-final.b64
  git am --3way < calder.patch
  git rev-parse "HEAD^{tree}"  # ULTIMATE PROOF — MUST print fc4f09a632c291d1998e18c1034245981bb57aa5

Then the standard gates in order:
  corepack pnpm install
  corepack pnpm -r --filter './packages/*' run build
  corepack pnpm -r --if-present test              # expect ~242 passed, 0 failed
  (cd apps/dashboard && corepack pnpm run build)  # expect clean, no Type errors
  pip install --break-system-packages pytest
  python3 -m pytest sdks/python/tests -q          # expect 16 passed

Then push arena/01a0d6fe-calder and open the real PR to main (source
material for the body: docs/PHASE6-RE-AUDIT.md, docs/DECISIONS.md
ADR-040/041/042, ROADMAP Phase-6 block; title: "Phases 5-6 completion —
auth hardening, control truth pass, official SDK libraries").
Tell the user afterwards to delete courier branches transfer-tmp (+its PR)
and transfer-two.

Path 2 — you can't even view/copy the file

Say "viewer is completely dead" and I'll start printing the base64 in chat-sized chunks here (about 9 messages, you paste each chunk to the new session; it reassembles and verifies the same checksums). It's slow but needs literally nothing except the chat you already have.

Important anti-corruption details baked into both paths: three independent checkpoints (b64 file hash → patch size+hash → git tree hash fc4f09a6…) catch any truncation or mangling long before anything touches the repo, and the patch still applies conflict-free onto the new session's exact HEAD by construction.
